{"notes":[{"n":1,"lesson":"用动词 frame 表示“把某事呈现成某种样子”，比 say 更精准。","file":true,"phrase":"framed as","ended":"“This is more than I deserve from you,” — the way you <m>framed</m> it <m>as</m> “captain's integrity” makes it seem he's coming to terms with his fate. On top of that, he's accepting her as his mother and feeling grateful for her final care. Was there even a little regret for what he had done to her?","meaning":"把……表述成；把……呈现为","usage":"用于评论作品时说明作者如何呈现某个情节、台词或人物行为，语气比 said 更具分析性。比“you said”更精准，能直接说明这是作者的写法。","examples":[{"t":"The ending <m>framed</m> his surrender <m>as</m> duty, so it felt earned.","n":"结局把他的投降呈现为一种责任，所以让人觉得水到渠成。"},{"t":"The news <m>framed</m> the delay <m>as</m> a minor issue.","n":"新闻把这次延误说成是小问题。"},{"t":"She <m>framed</m> the move <m>as</m> a chance to grow.","n":"她把这次搬家说成是一个成长的机会。"}]},{"n":2,"lesson":"AO3 评论区的固定说法是 leave kudos，kudos 为复数。","file":true,"phrase":"leave kudos","ended":"<m>Kudos left</m>~","meaning":"给作品点赞（AO3 上的“喜欢”）","usage":"这是 AO3 读者的固定说法，指在作品页面留下 kudos，与留言 comment 不同。kudos 是复数，不说 kudo。","examples":[{"t":"I was so moved by this chapter that I <m>left</m> <m>kudos</m> and a long comment.","n":"这一章让我太感动了，我不仅点了赞还写了长长的评论。"},{"t":"Thanks for <m>leaving kudos</m> on my story, it made my day!","n":"谢谢你给我的文点赞，今天因此变得很开心！"},{"t":"She never <m>leaves kudos</m> on fics she hasn't finished reading.","n":"她从来不会在没读完的文上点赞。"}]}]}
